WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.610
Let's go from Texas to Arizona.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:06.759
One way to avoid cases is not to do any tests.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:12.880
One way to avoid opinions that you shouldn't
reopen your state yet is to fire the people

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.660
telling you not to reopen the state.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.730
And that is what Arizona Republican Governor
Doug Doocy did on Monday.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:24.449
Doocy said he is accelerating the reopening
of Arizona.

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:29.919
That seemed questionable based on the case
numbers, which, if you look, have a very definitive

00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:34.930
upward curve spiking to nearly a new high
yesterday, matched only by the numbers on

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.180
April 30th.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.090
So the cases are spiking.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.930
Deaths usually follow closely behind.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.340
And Doocy says let's open up.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.420
Well, income, the public health officials
who say, hey, you know, look at the numbers,

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.100
we can't really reopen right now.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.060
Doocy doesn't like it, so he fires them.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:58.170
Steve Bailey, the bureau chief for public
health statistics at the Arizona Department

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:04.600
of Health Services, says, quote, We've been
asked by department leadership to pause all

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.799
current work on projections and modeling.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:12.100
Yeah, pause it until the pandemic is gone
and then start modeling again how great the

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.340
numbers are.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.600
These are the people we should be listening
to.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.310
Now, the timing is suspect.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.490
The timing to me has Trump's fingerprints
all over it.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:25.499
And it seems to have Trump's pressure all
over it because remember that Trump was in

00:01:25.499 --> 00:01:28.799
Arizona on Tuesday and the day before Trump
shows up.

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:34.090
Doocy says, we're going to reverse course
from what I said last week, a week ago.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:39.039
The governor in Arizona seemed to be taking
the seriously extended the stay home owner

00:01:39.039 --> 00:01:43.450
stay at home order until May 15, said stay
at home is working, said the data clearly

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.150
point to not opening up yet.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:50.969
But then this week we learned Trump's going
to Arizona on Tuesday, does a bunch of grandstanding

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:53.950
about reopening and the great governor.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.390
Doocy, who is there and getting the economy
going again.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:02.530
And just hours before Trump went to Arizona
the day before, Doocy decides, hey, you know

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:03.530
what?

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:04.859
We are going to open more stuff.

00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:09.739
We don't need the public health officials
modeling the impact of reopening anymore.

00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:11.920
And it has Trump's fingerprints all over.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.830
It's speculative, but it's what we know Trump
does.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.489
Arizona not the only state that is starting
to do strange things.

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:21.640
We already talked about Texas five minutes
ago.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:28.080
We have reports that Florida or Florida, as
some say, is hiding corona virus deaths by

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.049
not reporting the cause of death.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.049
People are dying.

00:02:31.049 --> 00:02:35.069
The reporting that a death took place there,
not including the cause of death in the reports

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:36.069
to the media.

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:41.430
And publicly, we have reports that Ohio is
changing how it reports numbers from a five

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.760
day to a 21 day timeframe to make it seem
as though the numbers are going down.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:52.019
What I believe is going on here, and I believe
Donald Trump's past behavior and statements

00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:59.480
justify at least exploring this, is that the
efforts are becoming more about let's not

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.340
talk about the deaths.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:06.200
Let's not talk about anything that's going
on medically.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.349
Let's just insist we're past the peak.

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:10.870
And let's talk about reopening.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.830
Let's talk about CEOs and states and all of
this other states of opening businesses and

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.040
all of that.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:23.319
And as usual, the very thing the Trump administration
is accusing others of doing is what it seems

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:25.080
like they themselves are doing.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.940
Some use the term projection to describe this.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.500
We're hearing more and more that the Trump
administration is questioning whether the

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.560
death numbers are accurate or whether they
are higher than the real numbers.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:42.450
Meanwhile, what we're learning about are the
strategies being employed by the Trump administration

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:48.480
and by states to make it a case that the death
numbers are actually lower than what they

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.890
really are while insisting that the testing
is greater than what it actually is.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.400
Trump can keep repeating 2.2 million deaths.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:02.749
All he wants, but he for weeks said sixty
thousand sixty thousand, 60000.

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:05.549
We're now at 75000 yesterday.

00:04:05.549 --> 00:04:07.980
Twenty five hundred people died the day before.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.079
Roughly twenty five hundred people died.

00:04:10.079 --> 00:04:14.530
At this rate, we will be at one hundred thousand
cases in 10 days.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:15.829
And it's going to continue growing.

00:04:15.829 --> 00:04:17.409
And it's a fiasco.

00:04:17.409 --> 00:04:21.579
While Spain, Italy, France, many other countries
have it under control.

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:22.710
Don't take my word for it.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.590
Look at the data coming out of Italy, Spain
and France.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:30.210
So what do you do if you're the Trump administration
when you've lost control of the situation?

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.210
You just lie.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:34.210
You say the death toll is lower than what
we were told.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.210
And I'm doing a.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.900
Great job and testing is great.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:37.900
And we're opening up the country.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.811
It's a disaster and people will continue to
die.

